// 'Water Caustic' — Benedikt Bitterli (CC0, public domain; crediting
// the artist encouraged). A Cornell room flooded chest-high, one small
// brilliant area light over the rippled surface: the caustic-transport
// standard. Official pbrt-v4 export from
// https://benedikt-bitterli.me/resources/ — `scenes/corpus/fetch.sh
// water-caustic` materializes the source; this RON was bootstrapped
// once by `cenote-cli import
// sources/bitterli/water-caustic/scene-v4.pbrt` and is the source of
// truth — re-imports diff into scratch, never over it.
//
// Import fidelity: exact — the one dropped parameter is sppm's photon
// radius, cosmetic because the scene's native integrator (SPPM) is
// pbrt-side only. Convergence, not correctness, is the story here:
// everything under the surface is lit exclusively through the smooth
// dielectric, which next-event estimation cannot cross, so a
// unidirectional path tracer resolves the submerged half and its
// caustic slowly, through fireflies — budget tens of thousands of spp,
// where pbrt's SPPM gathers photons instead.
